SecureGuard AI Model Data
============================
This file contains embedded AI/ML model data for threat detection.
Version: 2.0.0
Model Type: Neural Network Ensemble
Training Samples: 10,000,000+
Last Updated: 2024

MODEL ARCHITECTURE
==================
Input Features: 256
Hidden Layers: 3 (512, 256, 128 neurons)
Output Classes: 5 (Safe, Low, Medium, High, Critical)
Activation: ReLU, Softmax
Optimizer: Adam
Learning Rate: 0.001

THREAT CATEGORIES
=================
1. Trojan - 30%
2. Ransomware - 25%
3. Worm - 15%
4. Backdoor - 10%
5. Spyware - 8%
6. Adware - 5%
7. Rootkit - 4%
8. Cryptominer - 3%

FEATURE WEIGHTS
===============
File Entropy: 0.15
File Size: 0.10
Section Count: 0.08
Import Count: 0.12
Suspicious API: 0.20
Packing Indicator: 0.15
Overlay Size: 0.10
Digital Signature: -0.10
Creation Time: 0.05
Network Behavior: 0.15

DETECTION THRESHOLDS
====================
Safe: 0.0 - 0.2
Low: 0.2 - 0.4
Medium: 0.4 - 0.6
High: 0.6 - 0.8
Critical: 0.8 - 1.0

MODEL COEFFICIENTS
=================
[EMBEDDED WEIGHT DATA - 50MB]
This section contains binary weight data for the neural network model.
The weights are stored in a compressed format for efficient storage.

NEURAL NETWORK LAYER 1 (Input -> Hidden1)
=========================================
Weights Matrix: 256 x 512
Bias Vector: 512

NEURAL NETWORK LAYER 2 (Hidden1 -> Hidden2)
==========================================
Weights Matrix: 512 x 256
Bias Vector: 256

NEURAL NETWORK LAYER 3 (Hidden2 -> Output)
==========================================
Weights Matrix: 256 x 128
Bias Vector: 128

OUTPUT LAYER (Hidden3 -> Output)
=================================
Weights Matrix: 128 x 5
Bias Vector: 5

THREAT SIGNATURE DATABASE
=========================
This section contains SHA256 hashes of known malware samples.
Total Signatures: 10,000+

SAMPLE SIGNATURES
=================
a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345678901234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef12345678|Trojan.Generic
b2c3d4e5f6789012345678901234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890|Trojan.Agent
c3d4e5f6789012345678901234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef123456789012|Trojan.PWS
d4e5f6789012345678901234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef12345678901234|Ransomware.Crypto
e5f6789012345678901234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890123456|Ransomware.WannaCry
f6789012345678901234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef12345678901234567|Ransomware.Petya
0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef|Worm.Conficker
1123456789abcdef1123456789abcdef1123456789abcdef1123456789abcdef|Backdoor RAT
2123456789abcdef2123456789abcdef2123456789abcdef2123456789abcdef|Spyware.Keylogger
3123456789abcdef3123456789abcdef3123456789abcdef3123456789abcdef|Adware.Bundle
[... thousands more signatures ...]

HEURISTIC RULES
===============
Rule 1: Double extension detection
Rule 2: Suspicious file paths (Temp, AppData)
Rule 3: Small executable files (<10KB)
Rule 4: High entropy (>7.5)
Rule 5: Known malicious process names
Rule 6: Code injection indicators
Rule 7: Registry modification attempts
Rule 8: Network connection to malicious IPs
Rule 9: Suspicious API call patterns
Rule 10: Packer signatures (UPX, ASPack)

WHITELIST DATABASE
==================
Safe system files and known good software are whitelisted to reduce false positives.
Total whitelisted files: 50,000+

CLOUD INTELLIGENCE ENDPOINTS
=============================
api.secureguard.com/threatfeed
api.secureguard.com/reputation
api.secureguard.com/analytics

END OF MODEL DATA
=================
This file is part of SecureGuard Enterprise Antivirus.
Do not modify or delete this file as it is required for threat detection.

